    "notes": "Q6053470 and OSM way 27705333 identify the bridge. Current PMTiles and the aerial views identify the longer continuation to the town landing and the bend over the Ergene. The 1,264.81 m length follows the combined PMTiles centerline. Edirne lists a surviving length of 1,272 m and 164 standing arches. The older 1,392 m and 174-arch figures are retained separately. The 164-bay schedule approximates individual spacings and arch profiles from the ordinary aerial and bank views. The current model covers the visible exterior. It leaves the native river, floodplain and nearby modern roads in place. The skyline preserves the four river openings and selected floodplain arch silhouettes. District shows 84 physical vaults. Street and close-up retain all 164. The model does not express operational access or restoration dates. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
